        <mxCell id="legend" value="&lt;b&gt;How to read this&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; PR 1 and PR 2 start together; they don&amp;#39;t depend on each other.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; PR 3, 4 and 5 can then run side by side (PR 4 needs both PR 1 and PR 2).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; PR 7 is the join point: it needs PR 1, 2, 4, 5 and 6.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Longest chain: PR 1 &amp;rarr; 3 &amp;rarr; 6 &amp;rarr; 7 &amp;rarr; 8 (5 PRs in sequence)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#CCCCCC;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
